{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TraceNilpotent","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TraceNilpotent","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Trace.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceForm_eq_zero_of_mul_isNilpotent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceForm_eq_zero_of_mul_isNilpotent","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TraceNilpotent.lean#L64-L71","doc":"**The regular trace form vanishes whenever the product is nilpotent\n(sorry-free).**  If `x * y` is nilpotent then `regTraceForm K A x y = 0`.\nFor an `x` in a nil two-sided ideal, `x * y` is always nilpotent,\ngiving the radical-annihilation step of the semisimplicity theorem\n(the two-sided-ideal plumbing is brick B3d, `qou-u181`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.trace_lmul_eq_zero_of_isNilpotent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.trace_lmul_eq_zero_of_isNilpotent","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TraceNilpotent.lean#L56-L62","doc":"**The regular trace of a nilpotent element vanishes (sorry-free).**\nA nilpotent `z` has nilpotent `lmul z`, whose `LinearMap.trace` is a\nnilpotent element of the field `K`, hence `0` (a field is reduced). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceForm","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TraceNilpotent.lean#L47-L52","doc":"**The regular trace form** `B(x, y) = trace(L_{xy})`, the trace of\nleft-multiplication by `x * y` as a `K`-linear endomorphism of `A`.\nDefined for any (possibly noncommutative) algebra — the\nnoncommutative analogue of `Algebra.traceForm`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.isNilpotent_lmul_of_isNilpotent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.isNilpotent_lmul_of_isNilpotent","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TraceNilpotent.lean#L39-L44","doc":"**Left multiplication by a nilpotent element is nilpotent\n(sorry-free).**  `lmul K A` is an algebra homomorphism into the\nendomorphism ring, so it carries `xⁿ = 0` to `(lmul x)ⁿ = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}